# Module Hub V3 — Redesign Walkthrough

## What Changed
Complete rewrite of [ModuleHub.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/ModuleHub.tsx) addressing feedback that text was too small and info wasn't significant.

### Key Design Changes

| Before (V2) | After (V3) |
|---|---|
| 8–11px font sizes everywhere | `text-sm` / `text-base` (14–16px) throughout |
| Tiny count badges only | Full stat pills with labels: "3 Assignments", "2 Tasks", "1 New" |
| No immediate context | **Next deadline shown prominently** with title, countdown, and urgency icon |
| Flat item lists | Expandable detail cards with bg, border, and padding for each item |

### Hierarchy Structure
1. **Module Card** — course code (16px bold), next deadline with icon + urgency styling, stat pills
2. **Category Section** — "Assignments" / "Tasks" / "Announcements" with count badge, auto-opens for ≤3 items
3. **Item Detail** — expandable card showing priority, time estimate, due date, notes, Canvas links

### Visual Treatment
- Urgency items get `bg-urgency-subtle` + `AlertTriangle` icon
- Module colour dot at 12px (was 8px)
- Detail cards use `bg-surface/50` inset panels with proper `rounded-xl` borders
- "Full Hub" and "Canvas" links in the expanded nav bar

## Validation
- TypeScript: ✅ Zero errors
